  "note": "Election of the whole council (12 seats at large) on 18 May 1955; 13 candidates stood and 12 were returned (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1955, p. 8). 75 per cent poll. Ashe's 345 is printed as such; it is still above the only defeated candidate, R. B. Price (291). The nomination report (Belfast News-Letter, 6 May 1955, p. 10) recorded 14 nominations, reduced to 13 by the withdrawal of James M'Cracken. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026)."
